        "original_id": "a2b43c40-09dd-55ed-b0fd-44157ce6f322",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Archie Andrews, John L. Goldwater, Bob Montana, Vic Bloom, Fiona Staples\n- Organizations: Archie Comics\n- Products: Archie, Archie Andrews radio series, The Archie Show, Archie's Weird Mysteries, North 40, DV8: Gods and Monsters, T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents, Saga\n- Topics: comic books, comic book artists\n\nFacts:\n- In 1941, John L. Goldwater, Bob Montana, and Vic Bloom created Archie Andrews.\n- Archie Andrews is the main character in an American comic book series published by Archie Comics.\n- Archie Andrews is also featured in the long-running \"Archie Andrews\" radio series, a syndicated comic strip, \"The Archie Show\", and \"Archie's Weird Mysteries\".\n- Archie is an ongoing comic book series, also known as Archie Comics, that features the Archie Comics character Archie Andrews.\n- Fiona Staples is a Canadian comic book artist known for work on \"North 40\", \"DV8: Gods and Monsters\", \"T.H.U.N.D.E.R. Agents\", \"Archie\", and \"Saga\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
